      "conflicts": [
        "Track A rejects the ordinary named FinalState reading as source-incompatible, while Track B retains it as a source-compatible sensitivity. The accepted normalized obligation is Track B: true root termination remains the adopted ledger reading, but the author NL ambiguity is retained rather than erased.",
        "Track B claims O_IMPLIES_P, but the executed _running_event_exit oracle only accepts a root-owned direct Power_Off carrier from each active root child to [*]. O permits a semantically equivalent same-RTC completion structure, including a leaf-local Power_Off exit followed by an eventless owner/root completion continuation, so O does not imply this P.",
        "P does not imply O either: the oracle records but does not reject guards, does not establish guard feasibility, event dispatch, reachability, priority, or RTC termination. The relation is therefore UNRELATED, not O_IMPLIES_P.",
        "The defective receipt correctly establishes completed P=false, but its generic reason says false can falsify O. That execution interpretation conflicts with the independently checked relation and is not accepted as an O counterexample."
      ],
      "reason": "Accepted normalized obligation: Track B. It preserves the runtime Power Off quantifier, root-termination response, one-RTC reading, and the source-compatible named-final sensitivity. The selected static property is not a sound necessary condition because its implementation requires one particular direct root-exit encoding that O does not require. The false receipt is valid evidence that the submitted artifact fails P, not evidence that P is equivalent to O or that P=false alone proves O=false.",
      "basis": "The author NL and ledger packet require a runtime Power Off response, while the native artifact declares exact running leaves and Power_Off identity. The oracle source checks only root-owner direct carriers to EXIT_STATE and ignores guard feasibility and execution semantics. The defective receipt is COMPLETED_BOOLEAN false with the event identity true and all three direct-consumer constituents false; the independently frozen control is true on all four constituents. Both semantic replay projections match byte-for-byte, and the control diff is limited to replacing the cold initial Power_Off carrier with two running-mode root-exit carriers.",
