      "conflicts": [
        "Track A retains disjunctive and conjunctive takeover obligations in parallel because the comma does not choose a connective; Track B selects disjunction as the adopted O. The author source does not resolve this difference, so the normalized hash used for review is Track A and pane5 arbitration is still needed before any single-connective gold claim.",
        "Track B admits that the source supplies no canonical event identifiers, yet P compares exact invented FCSTM tokens Human_Steering_Cmd and Brake_Pressed after an underscore normalization. A behaviorally valid encoding may use variables, guards, one typed driver-input event, or different identifiers, so these two typed inputs are not accepted as source/native identities required by O.",
        "The selected P requires independent event declarations and takeover consumers plus an eventless AutoFinal route. The retained conjunctive O does not imply those three independent routes, and even the disjunctive reading does not mandate this carrier shape or identifier vocabulary. O therefore does not imply P.",
        "P does not imply O because _has_takeover_route ignores guard feasibility, dispatch, priority, and RTC behavior. A statically matched carrier with an impossible guard can satisfy P while violating either response obligation.",
        "The positive control is a valid pre-result true control for P and the disjunctive representation, but it does not resolve or test the retained conjunctive sensitivity. The defective receipt's generic claim that P=false falsifies O is therefore rejected."
      ],
      "reason": "Accepted normalized obligation for this review: Track A, because it preserves both source-compatible connective readings and their common requirement that two event-like atoms and the AutoFinal state condition not be collapsed into one atomic event identity. Track B's disjunctive O requires pane5 arbitration and cannot be silently promoted. The selected source-static oracle additionally invents exact event tokens and a particular three-route encoding; neither the dual-reading O nor a representation-neutral disjunctive O entails those constraints. The completed false remains valid only for P.",
      "basis": "The source packet classifies this issue D1 and explicitly preserves both comma readings. The defective native model contains one combined event and no independent required tokens; all four event declaration/consumer checks and the state-route check are false while the AutoFinal identity check is true. The control creates the two exact tokens and three routes and completes true, with a matching deterministic replay. The oracle code confirms that it compares Event.name literally and accepts direct or eventless-continuation carrier shapes without checking guards or runtime semantics.",
