      "conflicts": [
        "Track A deliberately excludes a separate initial-transition cardinality rule, while Track B states an existential nonempty default-entry clause. The accepted normalized obligation is Track A. On both hash-bound artifacts the discrepancy is non-operative because the complete native root init_transitions inventory is independently proven to contain exactly lines 19 and 21; no uniqueness or maximum cardinality is inferred.",
        "The four-way S3/S5 property does not dynamically quantify over arbitrary future carriers; it is exact only under the frozen artifact hashes and the independently checked complete inventory assumption. It must not be generalized to a changed model without re-enumerating root.init_transitions.",
        "The defective S3 constituents are false while both S5 constituents are true. The parent false is therefore an event-attachment defect on both carriers, not evidence of a guard defect; the non-short-circuit receipt preserves this distinction.",
        "Child receipts list additional execution dependency hashes that are not direct artifacts in the Track C packet. No unenumerated bytes were read. The listed source_static branch, typed schemas, public pyfcstm model/projection, exact native inventory reconstruction, raw observations, and matching replay corroborate the bindings, but future packets should directly bind every receipt code_hash dependency."
      ],
      "reason": "Accepted normalized obligation: Track A. It checks every one of the two source-identified root initial carriers for trigger and guard absence and explicitly avoids adding the separate at-most-one cardinality rule. The native root init_transitions inventory is exactly transition:line:19 and transition:line:21 in both defective and control bytes; line 12 is owned by AutonomousMode. S3 and S5 exactly compare event-set emptiness and guard absence on each bound carrier, so the non-short-circuit four-way AND is equivalent to this artifact-scoped O without silently asserting uniqueness.",
      "basis": "The defective parent request binds four exact constituents. Both S3 raw receipts complete false with observed Power_On and Power_Off respectively; both S5 raw receipts complete true with empty counterexamples. The parent is COMPLETED_BOOLEAN false and includes all four results. The control changes only lines 19 and 21 by removing their events, preserves both carriers and their guards, and all four control constituents complete true. Native parsing independently confirms root.init_transitions contains only lines 19 and 21 in both artifacts, while line 12 is nested. Original and replay parent state/verdict and every child semantic projection hash match.",
